{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/yang/php/antlr/ticks_test.clj test/yang/php/antlr/linked_harness.cljc; cat src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/publication.cljc; rg -n 'site-set|site.set|signed|alias' src/cljc/yang/*publication* src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/yang/php/antlr/ticks_test.clj test/yang/php/antlr/linked_harness.cljc; cat src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/publication.cljc; rg -n 'site-set|site.set|signed|alias' src/cljc/yang/*publication* src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.php.antlr.ticks-test\n  (:require\n    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    [yang.php.antlr.cst :as cst]\n    [yang.php.antlr.e2e-harness :as h]\n    [yang.php.antlr.linked-harness :as lh]\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p7b :as p7b]))\n\n\n(deftest tick-fixtures-test\n  (doseq [{:keys [id source out units]} p7b/fixtures\n          :when (nil? units)]\n    (testing (name id)\n      (is (= out (:php/out (h/run-raw (str \"<?php \" p7b/prologue source))))))))\n\n\n(deftest include-handoff-test\n  (let [{:keys [source units out]} (last p7b/fixtures)\n        packets (update-vals (assoc units \"main.php\" (str \"<?php \" p7b/prologue source))\n                             cst/parse-source)\n        result (lh/run-fixture packets \"main.php\" {})]\n    (doseq [[vm value] (:values result)]\n      (is (= out (h/latin1->text (:php/out value))) (name vm)))))\n(ns yang.php.antlr.linked-harness\n  \"The linked profile's composition for the PHP tests (P6, docs/design/\n   yang.php.md section 11): the namespace that requires this is the\n   publisher of `php`, so it publishes the module once per process into one\n   in-memory content store, publishes a fixture's non-entry units beside it\n   bottom-up, and serves them to the entry unit's run over a\n   `yin.vm.linker.interpreter` composition under `:trusted` derivation.\n\n   A linked run builds the entry unit's task on one of the three vector VMs\n   with a link pair, then runs the VM and serves the pair alternately until\n   the VM stops blocking, as the REPL's drive does. The AST walker is not a\n   backend here: its link of `php` is refused until L-b.\"\n  (:require\n    [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    [yang.core.call :as call]\n    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as portable]\n    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n    [yang.php.antlr.publication :as publication]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n    [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]\n    [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n    [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n    [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n    [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\n    [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n(defn registry\n  \"The host registry a linked PHP composition registers: the `require`\n   handlers, then `cell`, `data` and `integer` under the portable limits.\"\n  []\n  (portable/linked-registry))\n\n\n(def published\n  \"`yang.call` and `php` published once into their own content store.\"\n  (delay\n    (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n          call-result (publish/publish-module! store (call/module-spec (registry)))\n          result (publish/publish-module! store (prelude/module-spec (registry)\n                                                                     (:address call-result)))]\n      {:store store,\n       :result result,\n       :address (:address result),\n       :call-address (:address call-result)})))\n\n\n(defn publish-units!\n  \"`units` (`[{:name path :packet p :strict-types b}]`) published into\n   `php`'s own content store, where its pinned requirement already lives:\n   `publication/publish-units!`'s answer.\"\n  [units]\n  (publication/publish-units! (:store @published) (registry) (:address @published) units))\n\n\n(defn source\n  \"The serving composition over the published store: `name-env` names `php`\n   and each published module, derivation `:trusted`, the test being the\n   publisher.\"\n  [name-env]\n  (link/composition {:content-store (:store @published),\n                     :name-env (merge {'php (:address @published),\n                                       'yang.call (:call-address @published)} name-env),\n                     :derivation :trusted}))\n\n\n(def backends\n  \"Each vector backend's root task over a program AST and composition.\"\n  {:semantic (fn [ast opts]\n               (semantic/load-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\n                                  (vm/ast->datoms ast)\n                                  vm/ast-contract)),\n   :stack (fn [ast opts]\n            (dvm/create-vm (:image (derive/stack-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))))\n                           (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract))),\n   :register (fn [ast opts]\n               (rvm/create-vm (derive/register-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast)))\n                              (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract)))})\n\n\n(defn composition\n  \"A task's composition over `modules` and the link `pair`.\"\n  [modules pair]\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream,\n   :capability-secret tu/secret,\n   :secret-source (fn [origin] (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin))),\n   :primitives vm/primitives,\n   :modules modules,\n   :link-request (:requests pair),\n   :link-response (:responses pair)})\n\n\n(defn drive\n  \"Run `task` and serve `pair` from `src` alternately until the task stops\n   blocking, at most 80 rounds. Returns `[task pair]`.\"\n  [task pair src]\n  (loop [task (vm/run task)\n         pair pair\n         i 0]\n    (if (and (vm/blocked? task) (< i 80))\n      (let [pair (:pair (link/serve {:pair pair, :source src}))]\n        (recur (vm/run task) pair (inc i)))\n      [task pair])))\n\n\n(defn run-linked\n  \"The finished task of the linked program `ast` on `backend`, served from\n   `src`. A refused link surfaces as the program's own diagnostics.\"\n  [backend ast src]\n  (let [pair (link/make-pair)\n        task ((get backends backend) ast (composition (registry) pair))]\n    (first (drive task pair src))))\n\n\n(defn name-env\n  \"The name environment naming every published module of `result`\n   (`publish-units!`'s answer): module symbol to address.\"\n  [result]\n  (merge (into {} (map (fn [[path address]] [(lower/path-module-symbol path) address]))\n               (:addresses result))\n         (:bundles result)))\n\n\n(defn run-fixture\n  \"`{backend value}` for the multi-unit fixture `units` (`{path packet}`,\n   the entry unit `main`, default `lower/entry-path`) on the three vector\n   VMs: the non-entry units are published bottom-up, the entry unit\n   lowered `:linked` and run. `value` is `run-main`'s map.\"\n  ([units] (run-fixture units lower/entry-path {}))\n  ([units main opts]\n   (let [entry (get units main)\n         others (cond-> (mapv (fn [[path packet]] {:name path, :packet packet})\n                              (dissoc units main))\n                  (:class-map opts) (conj (assoc (:class-map opts) :name lower/classmap-name)))\n         result (publish-units! others)]\n     (when-not (= :ok (:status result))\n       (throw (ex-info \"fixture units failed to publish\" {:result result})))\n     (let [{:keys [ast warnings]}\n           (lower/lower-program entry\n                                (cond-> (merge {:prelude :linked,\n                                                :path main,\n                                                :paths (when (:computed? opts) (keys (:addresses result)))}\n                                               (dissoc opts :computed? :src :request))\n                                  (:class-map opts) (assoc :class-map true)\n                                  (some? (:request opts)) (assoc :request-node\n                                                                 (portable/request-node (:request opts)))))\n           src (or (:src opts) (source (name-env result)))]\n       {:warnings warnings,\n        :values (into {}\n                      (map (fn [k] [k (vm/value (run-linked k ast src))]))\n                      (keys backends))}))))\n(ns yang.php.antlr.publication\n  \"P6 (docs/design/yang.php.md section 11): a set of compiled PHP units\n   published as linker modules. The ordering, SCC bundling and publish loop\n   are `yang.core.publication`'s; this namespace supplies the PHP hooks: the\n   includes `lower/imported-unit-names` folds, the `lower/module-spec` and\n   `lower/scc-module-specs` emitters and site sets; no binder table.\n\n   A unit is `{:name path :packet p :strict-types b}`, `path` its normalized\n   relative path; the optional class map entry is `{:name \\\"$classmap\\\"\n   :classes {class path} :paths [path ...]}`. Name assertions stay the\n   linker's: this namespace publishes content, it signs nothing.\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.core.publication :as core]\n    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.php.antlr.siteset :as siteset]\n    [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]))\n\n\n(defn- class-map?\n  \"The autoload class map entry of a unit set, `{:name \\\"$classmap\\\" :classes\n   {class path} :paths [path ...]}`: it imports every path it lists, so it\n   publishes last and an unpublished path is refused by name (plan P6 R9).\"\n  [unit]\n  (= lower/classmap-name (:name unit)))\n\n\n(defn- config\n  [publish-fn]\n  {:imported-names (fn [{:keys [name packet], :as unit}]\n                     (if (class-map? unit)\n                       (lower/classmap-paths unit)\n                       (lower/imported-unit-names packet {:path name}))),\n   :module-spec (fn [registry {:keys [name packet strict-types], :as unit} php-address deps]\n                  (if (class-map? unit)\n                    (lower/classmap-spec registry unit php-address deps)\n                    (lower/module-spec registry packet\n                                       {:path name,\n                                        :strict-types strict-types,\n                                        :php-address php-address,\n                                        :deps deps}))),\n   :scc-module-specs lower/scc-module-specs,\n   :site-set siteset/publish!,\n   :alias-site-set true,\n   :binder-table nil,\n   :refusal-ns \"yang.php\",\n   :publish-fn publish-fn})\n\n\n(defn publication-order\n  \"Dependency-first names, retaining the input order for acyclic units.\n   Cyclic components appear as sorted member vectors in :order, one\n   publication step per SCC. An include edge no unit and no `published`\n   entry supplies is refused `:yang.php/unpublished-import` by name.\"\n  [units published]\n  (core/publication-order (config publish/publish-module!) units published))\n\n\n(defn publish-units!\n  \"Publish `units` into the content store `handle` over the host registry\n   `registry`, `php` pinned at `php-address` and each include outside the\n   set at its address in `published` ({path address}), in\n   `publication-order`. Answers `{:status :ok :addresses {path address}\n   :bundles {bundle-symbol address}}`, or the first refusal:\n   `publication-order`'s before anything is written, else\n   `publish-module!`'s with a string `:unit`.\"\n  ([handle registry php-address units]\n   (publish-units! handle registry php-address units {}))\n  ([handle registry php-address units published]\n   (publish-units! handle registry php-address units published publish/publish-module!))\n  ([handle registry php-address units published publish-fn]\n   (core/publish-units! (config publish-fn) handle registry php-address units published)))\nzsh:1: no matches found: src/cljc/yang/*publication*\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"The producer publishes site-set records separately from manifests, so the missing piece is a discoverable signed binding before derivation can be trusted. I’m tracing the existing auxiliary-record publication and discovery path, including how it handles aliases and dependency addresses."}}
